tasks.goal:
A publish panel in the editor:
- shows a dry run with what becomes visible and the blast radius;
- runs entry.publish, or variant.release followed by a placement window;
- creates a placement with the NodePicker, a slug and a locale;
- schedules a window and unpublishes.

A Preview tab reads a new query entry.preview. It encodes the draft or a chosen revision through the record codecs at public access, exactly as delivery would. It shows a structured document view at reading width, with locale and width switches.

Preview never writes and never touches the fragment store.

A singleton type's nav entry opens its one entry, per site with the site switcher for site scope, or it offers to create the entry.

A menu field input edits a tree of up to 3 levels with the replicator's patterns:
- drag and keyboard reorder;
- indent and outdent;
- items with the link input;
- broken links marked.

Design round 2 (Globals, Menu) is still pending, so the input follows the approved round-1 Editor patterns.

A new workbench fixture type, routable and draft-release, is added as one schema file plus its generated code and migration. It uses nested blocks, rich text with an entry link and a set, a relation, a link, money, properties, a when condition and a layout.

A Browser test then:
1. creates the entry, edits it and reorders its blocks;
2. releases and publishes it;
3. previews it in the panel;
4. reads it from GET /v1/resolve.

The task's commit changes no file under packages/ or js/. The reference scenario with a real editor (GUARDRAILS 8) is recorded under 'Til review af Sylvester' as review pending.
